PART B -- THE RECORD: were the recorded closures of an ADDED sector or of an EMERGENT one?
======================================================================================================================
B.1  The named no-go (g03w-g04j; L14 in FINDINGS).  In the deposited action (THE_ACTION_2026-09-05 sections 1-3)
     the MOND force is 2(2-K_B) J^mu d_mu phi with the kernel J(Y) carrying a0; the condensate K(Q) = K_2 (Q-Q_0)^2
     supplies dust whose amplitude 'is a free cosmological initial datum'.  The static law div[mu grad Phi] = 4 pi G rho
     contains NO dust parameter.  g04j's own docstring: 'one mechanism that keeps a cold-on-cluster-scales fluid OUT of
     galaxies has never been run'.  g04f: 'the candidate's dark sector as a single thermal species'.  Every one of those
     closures is of a component ADDED to a kernel that already works at zero dust -- hypothesis (a) HOLDS for them.
  [PASS] B1  the named dark-sector no-go (g03w-g04j) closed a sector ADDED to a kernel that works at zero dust: hypothesis (a) holds for every theory it examined, so it does NOT cover the emergent class   (the action's a0 sits in J(Y); the dust amplitude is a free initial datum; the static law has no dust parameter)

B.2  The UNNAMED record: condensate_pincer_2026/superfluid_route_gates_2026.py (2026-09-02, 4 checks, 0 FAIL) took
     'the dark field IS MOND' -- the Berezhiani-Khoury class, condensing inside galaxies and producing the a0 force
     there as a phonon -- and closed it on the COSMOLOGICAL BACKGROUND: G2, any self-interaction that thermalises a
     halo thermalised the background earlier (Gamma/H grows as (1+z)^2.5) where n lambda_dB^3 >> 1, so the background
     condensed and, with T/T_c constant under expansion, stays condensed; G3, the condensed background's sound speed
     c_s^2 ~ (rho/rho_core)^2 c_s,core^2 is relativistic at recombination for any core the phonons could hold up.
     Reproduced at A4.  That IS a recorded closure of the emergent class -- on one gate, under one extrapolation
     (the P ~ rho^3 equation of state carried to recombination densities, which the class's own literature flags as
     the regime where its EFT is not established).  It says nothing about lensing, the Solar System, the EFE, the
     Gaia arms, the preferred frame, or whether the anomaly is spent once.  Those are run below; they do not lean on it.
  [PASS] B2  the recorded emergent-class closure is cosmological and reproduces; the theorem-driven gates are untested in the record   (scope: background phase + EOS extrapolation; gates 1-7 of the brief never run on the class)
      pricing the escape: a core at 6e+03 x mean held up at c_s = 200 km/s has c_s^2(z_rec)/c^2 = 4.4e-7 x (2.0e+05)^(n-1);
        the loose GDM ceiling 1e-5 is met only for n <= 1.26 -- softer than any pressure that could hold the core (the phonon law needs n = 3)

======================================================================================================================
PART C -- HYPOTHESIS (a) FOR THE EMERGENT CLASS, derived from the phonon action
======================================================================================================================
The BK15 phonon EFT:  L = P(X) - (alpha Lambda/M_Pl) theta rho_b,   P = (2 Lambda (2m)^{3/2}/3) X sqrt|X|,
X = mu_loc - (grad theta)^2/(2m).  In the gradient-dominated (MOND) regime |X| = (grad theta)^2/2m.
      P_X/m = 2*Lambda*gradtheta;  spherical solution |grad theta| = sqrt(alpha M_b/(8 pi M_Pl r^2));  a_theta = (alpha Lambda/M_Pl)|grad theta|
      a_theta^2 / a_N = Lambda**2*alpha**3/M_Pl   =  a0_ph  (BK15's scale, recovered symbolically)
  [PASS] C1  the phonon force is a_theta = sqrt(a0_ph a_N) with a0_ph = alpha^3 Lambda^2/M_Pl, derived from the action (control on the algebra)
      the condensate density in the gradient-dominated regime is rho_SF = m P_X = 2*Lambda*gradtheta*m**2  (BK15's gradient-locked density)

     HYPOTHESIS (a) asks for the force with the cold component OFF.  With no condensate there is no phonon: theta is
     the Goldstone of the condensate's U(1), P(X) is the condensate's own pressure, and the coupling alpha Lambda theta rho_b
     acts on baryons only where theta exists.  Set rho_SF -> 0: P_X -> 0 with it (rho_SF = m P_X above), the flux
     coefficient vanishes, and the EOM has no solution carrying a force -- A_K == 0, not sqrt(g_bar a0).  L61's (H-b)
     'with A_X = 0 the theory reproduces the observed relation' is therefore FALSE for the class, and the proof step
     g_obs = g_bar + A_K that turns g_pred - g_obs into A_X cannot be taken.  The theorem's conclusion does not follow.
  [PASS] C2  hypothesis (a) FAILS for the emergent class: with the condensate off the phonon force is identically zero, so (H-b) is violated and the excess-spent-once conclusion does not go through   (A_K(rho_SF = 0) = 0; the class is outside L61's hypotheses, exactly as the brief conjectured)
     What replaces (H-b): g_pred = g_bar + g_SF + a_theta, with g_SF the condensate's OWN Newtonian pull and a0_ph a
     Lagrangian constant that the literature FITS (A7b).  Whether the anomaly is spent once is now a computation, PART D.

======================================================================================================================
PART D -- SPENT ONCE OR TWICE?  The condensate's own pull on SPARC, at the CMB's abundance
======================================================================================================================
The cold component is present in galaxies at the abundance-matched amount (L61's M200, the CMB's Omega_c h^2 through
the stellar-to-halo relation), but its PROFILE is the theory's: inside the thermalised region it is the n = 1/2
polytrope of A.4 (BFK18's finite-temperature picture), and in BK15's zero-temperature MOND regime it is the
gradient-locked rho_SF = 2 Lambda m^2 |grad theta|.  Both are computed at every SPARC point, both parameter sets.

